@ 1:6  venn-|beta
  1:1-1:10 "venn-beta"
  | **`venn-beta`**
  |
  | `venn-beta`: starts a venn diagram.
@ 2:5  ti|tle Overlap
  2:3-2:8 "title"
  | **`title`**
  |
  | `title <text>`: the diagram title, the rest of the line; one pair of surrounding quotes is removed, as in `title "Team overlap"`.
@ 3:4  s|et A
  3:3-3:6 "set"
  | **`set`**
  |
  | `set <id>`: a set, with an optional `[label]` and `:size` (10 by default), as in `set A["Alpha"]:20`.
@ 4:5  un|ion A,A
  4:3-4:8 "union"
  | **`union`**
  |
  | `union <id>,<id>…`: the overlap of two or more sets declared before it, with an optional `[label]` and `:size` (10 / n² for n sets by default), as in `union A,B["Both"]:2`.
@ 5:7  te|xt a1
  5:5-5:9 "text"
  | **`text`**
  |
  | `text <id>` on an indented line right under a `set` or `union` (or another such line): a text node in its area, which takes that statement's sets.
@ 6:6  sty|le A fill: red
  6:3-6:8 "style"
  | **`style`**
  |
  | `style <ids> key: value, …`: the `fill`, `fill-opacity`, `stroke`, `stroke-width` and `color` of a set, an overlap or a text node, as in `style A,B fill: #f00`.
@ 7:5  te|xt A t1
  7:3-7:7 "text"
  | **`text`**
  |
  | `text <ids> <id>`: a text node in the area of those sets, with an optional `[label]` (not after an id that is a number), as in `text A,B t1["In both"]`.
@ 8:8  set B|["Label"]
  8:7-8:8 "B"
  | **`B`** set · Label
  |
  | Size 10 (the default).
@ 9:9  set C:|10
  none
